{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we first need to understand the sequence \\( T = \\{t_0, t_1, t_2, \\ldots\\} \\) defined by \\( t_0 = 0 \\), \\( t_1 = 1 \\), and \\( t_n = t_{n-2} + t_{n-1} \\) for all integers \\( n > 1 \\). This is a Fibonacci-like sequence, and we need to determine the values of \\( t_n \\mod 7 \\).\n\nLet's compute the first few terms of the sequence modulo 7:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nt_0 &\\equiv 0 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_1 &\\equiv 1 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_2 &\\equiv t_0 + t_1 \\equiv 0 + 1 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_3 &\\equiv t_1 + t_2 \\equiv 1 + 1 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_4 &\\equiv t_2 + t_3 \\equiv 1 + 2 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_5 &\\equiv t_3 + t_4 \\equiv 2 + 3 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_6 &\\equiv t_4 + t_5 \\equiv 3 + 5 \\equiv 8 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_7 &\\equiv t_5 + t_6 \\equiv 5 + 1 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_8 &\\equiv t_6 + t_7 \\equiv 1 + 6 \\equiv 7 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_9 &\\equiv t_7 + t_8 \\equiv 6 + 0 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_{10} &\\equiv t_8 + t_9 \\equiv 0 + 6 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_{11} &\\equiv t_9 + t_{10} \\equiv 6 + 6 \\equiv 12 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_{12} &\\equiv t_{10} + t_{11} \\equiv 6 + 5 \\equiv 11 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_{13} &\\equiv t_{11} + t_{12} \\equiv 5 + 4 \\equiv 9 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_{14} &\\equiv t_{12} + t_{13} \\equiv 4 + 2 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_{15} &\\equiv t_{13} + t_{14} \\equiv 2 + 6 \\equiv 8 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_{16} &\\equiv t_{14} + t_{15} \\equiv 6 + 1 \\equiv 7 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{7}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nWe observe that the sequence repeats every 16 terms. Therefore, \\( t_n \\equiv t_{n \\mod 16} \\pmod{7} \\).\n\n","prefix_end":1524,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1156,1184,311,3535,279,8500,17767,350,284,1124,90,83,62,15,11,259,62,16,11,259,62,1