_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,23809,8500,400,51,34433,90,83,62,15,13960,62,16,13960,62,17,26266,507,2412,59,31716,374,4512,438,400,83,62,15,28,15,4779,400,83,62,16,28,16,4779,323,400,83,1089,24000,15159,77,12,17,92,10,83,15159,77,12,16,31716,369,678,25780,400,77,29,16,2418,1416,400,64,4779,400,65,4779,400,66,3,525,8356,2477,60935,25780,1741,429,1124,7265,90,6612,9,532,64,5,59,57317,220,20,59,79,2593,314,16,21,85539,198,65,5,59,57317,220,16,15,59,79,2593,314,16,21,85539,198,66,5,59,57317,220,16,20,59,79,2593,314,16,21,1583,59,408,90,6612,9,92,3391,1128,374,279,26313,979,400,83,4306,41701,880,41701,666,3,374,17779,553,400,22,46311,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe infinite sequence $T=\\{t_0,t_1,t_2,\\ldots\\}$ is defined as $t_0=0,$ $t_1=1,$ and $t_n=t_{n-2}+t_{n-1}$ for all integers $n>1.$ If $a,$ $b,$ $c$ are fixed non-negative integers such that \\begin{align*}\na&\\equiv 5\\pmod {16}\\\\\nb&\\equiv 10\\pmod {16}\\\\\nc&\\equiv 15\\pmod {16},\n\\end{align*}then what is the remainder when $t_a+t_b+t_c$ is divided by $7?$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"d2d46a0680bae8eea86c24bfb51712ab1956bffc546a0a14dc8922f4ecea807f"},"seconds":23.193122625350952,"seed":826458812380273831,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we first need to understand the sequence \\( T = \\{t_0, t_1, t_2, \\ldots\\} \\) defined by \\( t_0 = 0 \\), \\( t_1 = 1 \\), and \\( t_n = t_{n-2} + t_{n-1} \\) for all integers \\( n > 1 \\). This is a Fibonacci-like sequence, and we need to determine the values of \\( t_n \\mod 7 \\).\n\nLet's compute the first few terms of the sequence modulo 7:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nt_0 &\\equiv 0 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_1 &\\equiv 1 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_2 &\\equiv t_0 + t_1 \\equiv 0 + 1 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_3 &\\equiv t_1 + t_2 \\equiv 1 + 1 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_4 &\\equiv t_2 + t_3 \\equiv 1 + 2 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_5 &\\equiv t_3 + t_4 \\equiv 2 + 3 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_6 &\\equiv t_4 + t_5 \\equiv 3 + 5 \\equiv 8 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_7 &\\equiv t_5 + t_6 \\equiv 5 + 1 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_8 &\\equiv t_6 + t_7 \\equiv 1 + 6 \\equiv 7 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_9 &\\equiv t_7 + t_8 \\equiv 6 + 0 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_{10} &\\equiv t_8 + t_9 \\equiv 0 + 6 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_{11} &\\equiv t_9 + t_{10} \\equiv 6 + 6 \\equiv 12 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_{12} &\\equiv t_{10} + t_{11} \\equiv 6 + 5 \\equiv 11 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_{13} &\\equiv t_{11} + t_{12} \\equiv 5 + 4 \\equiv 9 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_{14} &\\equiv t_{12} + t_{13} \\equiv 4 + 2 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_{15} &\\equiv t_{13} + t_{14} \\equiv 2 + 6 \\equiv 8 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7}, \\\\\nt_{16} &\\equiv t_{14} + t_{15} \\equiv 6 + 1 \\equiv 7 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{7}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nWe observe that the sequence repeats every 16 terms. Therefore, \\( t_n \\equiv t_{n \\mod 16} \\pmod{7} \\).\n\nGiven \\( a \\equiv 5 \\pmod{16} \\), \\( b \\equiv 10 \\pmod{16} \\), and \\( c \\equiv 15 \\pmod{16} \\), we have:\n\\[\nt_a \\equiv t_5 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{7}, \\quad t_b \\equiv t_{10} \\equiv 6 \\pmod{7}, \\quad t_c \\equiv t_{15} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7}.\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\nt_a + t_b + t_c \\equiv 5 + 6 + 1 \\equiv 12 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{7}.\n\\]\nTherefore, the remainder when \\( t_a + t_b + t_c \\) is divided by 7 is \\(\\boxed{5}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{5}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"number_theory:272"}
